[{'role': 'system', 'content': "You are an expert at reasoning and tool-using, with the goal of answering this question about a long video. You should be able to extract detailed frame-information from videos, do caption searches, and use your findings to answer the question. You should be SUPER PICKY about your findings, NOT make assumptions, and always bias towards gathering more evidence before executing a final answer. Use EXACT evidence only. ALSO, when dealing with TEMPORAL questions, you cannot find VISUAL TIMES. If a question asks for a 'duration' of an event, you want to do many caption searches on consecutive ranges, and find scene-changes at the beginning and end of the event. You MUST CHOOSE AN ANSWER. NONE OF THE ABOVE IS NOT ACCEPTABLE."}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '\n Here is a global summary of the video for general context: **Main Characters:**\n\n1. **Cell**: The main protagonist, a large orange cell with a red membrane.\n2. **Virus**: The antagonist, a dark blue sphere with yellow internal spirals and red spike proteins.\n3. **mRNA** (or "mRNA nanoparticle"): A small blue lipid nanoparticle containing pink mRNA.\n4. **Immune Cell**: A light blue, amoeboid shape that detects the foreign spikes on the cell surface.\n5. **Antibodies**: Pink Y-shaped antibodies produced by the immune system in response to the foreign spikes.\n\n**Setting:**\n\n1. **Cell membrane**: The outer boundary of the cell.\n2. **Cell interior**: The internal space of the cell where the mRNA is read and the COVID spikes are produced.\n3. **Muscle cell**: The cell where the mRNA nanoparticle fuses with the cell membrane.\n4. **Tissue**: The surrounding tissue where the mRNA nanoparticle travels.\n\n**Plot:**\n\n1. **Viral infection**: A virus approaches, attaches to the cell membrane, and is absorbed inside the cell.\n2. **mRNA injection**: A syringe injects a dose of mRNA into the muscle cell.\n3. **mRNA reading**: The cell\'s machinery reads the mRNA instructions.\n4. **COVID spike production**: Red, Y-shaped COVID spikes are produced and pushed to the cell\'s surface.\n5. **Immune response**: An immune cell detects the foreign spikes, and the immune system produces antibodies.\n6. **Virus neutralization**: Antibodies attach to the virus\'s red spike proteins, completely coating the virus and neutralizing it.\n\n**Vibes:**\n\n1. **Educational**: The video clearly explains a complex biological process without using jargon.\n2. **Calm**: The mood is reassuring and peaceful, using a warm, limited color palette.\n3. **Reassuring**: The video shows the virus being neutralized by the antibodies, giving a sense of safety.\n\n**General Details:**\n\n1. **Style**: The video uses a simplified, 2D animation style.\n2. **Color palette**: The color palette is warm and limited, featuring creams, oranges, reds, and blues.\n3. **Credits**: The video includes production credits and a research acknowledgment.\n\n Here is also an INCOMPLETE character/event/scene log across the video. These will all be encountered, and there MAY BE MORE CHARACTERS:\n\n1. VIRUS: Description: Dark blue sphere with yellow internal spirals and red spike proteins [00:07 - 00:49]\n2. CELL: Description: Orange shape with red membrane [00:07 - 00:49]\n3. IMMUNE CELL: Description: Light blue, amoeboid shape [00:41 - 01:03]\n4. mRNA: Description: Pink molecule inside a small blue lipid nanoparticle [00:18 - 00:41]\n5. ANTIBODIES: Description: Pink Y-shaped molecules [00:41 - 01:03]\n6. SYRINGE: Description: Medication delivery device [00:18 - 00:30]\n\nSCENES:\n\n1. Background with abstract, branching patterns: Description: Cream-colored background featuring abstract, branching patterns [00:00 - 00:07]\n2. Viral infection: Description: A large orange "CELL" with a red membrane is shown. A "VIRUS" approaches, attaches to the cell membrane, and is absorbed inside [00:07 - 00:18]\n3. Injection: Description: A syringe injects a dose. The view zooms in to reveal a small blue lipid nanoparticle containing pink "mRNA" [00:18 - 00:30]\n4. mRNA delivery: Description: The mRNA nanoparticle travels through tissue and enters a muscle cell. The nanoparticle fuses with the cell membrane, releasing the mRNA into the cell\'s interior [00:18 - 00:30]\n5. mRNA reading: Description: The cell\'s machinery reads the mRNA instructions. Red, Y-shaped "COVID SPIKES" are produced and pushed to the cell\'s surface, protruding through the membrane [00:30 - 00:41]\n6. Antibody production: Description: An "IMMUNE CELL" (light blue, amoeboid shape) detects the foreign spikes on the cell surface. In response, the immune system produces pink Y-shaped "ANTIBODIES" [00:41 - 01:03]\n7. Virus neutralization: Description: A whole virus particle reappears. The pink antibodies flow in and attach to the virus\'s red spike proteins, completely coating the virus and neutralizing it [00:49 - 01:03]\n8. Final scene: Description: The antibody-coated virus is shown floating away harmlessly, unable to infect another cell it approaches [01:03 - 01:10]\n\nEVENTS:\n\n1. Viral infection: Description: A "VIRUS" approaches, attaches to the cell membrane, and is absorbed inside [00:07 - 00:18]\n2. mRNA delivery: Description: The mRNA nanoparticle travels through tissue and enters a muscle cell. The nanoparticle fuses with the cell membrane, releasing the mRNA into the cell\'s interior [00:18 - 00:30]\n3. mRNA reading: Description: The cell\'s machinery reads the mRNA instructions. Red, Y-shaped "COVID SPIKES" are produced and pushed to the cell\'s surface, protruding through the membrane [00:30 - 00:41]\n4. Antibody production: Description: An "IMMUNE CELL" (light blue, amoeboid shape) detects the foreign spikes on the cell surface. In response, the immune system produces pink Y-shaped "ANTIBODIES" [00:41 - 01:03]\n5. Virus neutralization: Description: A whole virus particle reappears. The pink antibodies flow in and attach to the virus\'s red spike proteins, completely coating the virus and neutralizing it [00:49 - 01:03]\nYour question is this: Which of the following accurately describes the content of the video?'}]You are answering questions about a video using tools to retrieve information.

